From 9462a2c5669875576308e4555822cf86ecca42a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:42:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(import): stop a STEP pass after a few runaway faces

Every face and edge meter of one shell's tessellation pass now shares one
pass budget. Each meter counts its first refusal there; at PASS_TRIPS (3)
trips the pass stops, every meter answers its fixed point, and the pass is
refused by name, saying it stopped. A stopped pass is never continuous, so
no coarser mesh is kept. A hostile shell of many runaway faces now costs at
most 3 caps plus one per worker thread, not one cap per face.

Meter moves to step_meter.rs (400-line law) beside the new Pass.

Fixes #1599

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
